Content: an embedder's own input to the frames of a page, as a window's.

zebkit's off-screen views (<zebkit/offscreen.h>) send the application's
mouse, wheel and keys to the page with RenderWidgetHost::Forward*, to the
page's main widget. A frame in another process (another site, or a
sandboxed frame of an opaque origin) has a widget of its own there: the
main frame's renderer only has a placeholder for it, and the frame got no
clicks, hover, selection drags, scrolls or keys. A window's events go
through the WebContents' RenderWidgetHostInputEventRouter instead
(RenderWidgetHostViewAura, RenderWidgetHostViewMac, CEF's off-screen view):
it hit tests the frames, keeps a pressed button's frame until release,
sends enter and leave between frames, and keeps a scroll on its frame; keys
go to GetFocusedRenderWidgetHost(). content/public/browser/zebkit_input.h
gives an embedder the same entry points.

The cursor hook (patches/1021) is called with the cursor the root view
shows (DisplayCursor(), the CursorManager's choice of the frame under the
mouse) rather than whatever widget last set one, which left a frame's
cursor after the mouse had left the frame.

